WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.080
Follow up, stay honest, and track your numbers.

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:07.480
This is the video for Module 3 of Client Acquisition Basics.

3
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:15.480
Silence after your first message rarely means no. Business owners are busy, and messages get buried.

4
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:23.960
Many freelancers send one message and give up. A planned follow-up shows persistence without becoming a nuisance.

5
00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:31.930
Your outreach must stay honest and respect people's data, because one discovered lie can close many doors.

6
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.740
And a few simple numbers show you exactly where to improve.

7
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.080
Day 0 is your first message.

8
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.550
On day 3 or 4, send one or two lines that bring it back to the top.

9
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:52.880
On day 10, send something useful with no strings attached, like a tip or the sample you offered.

10
00:00:54.130 --> 00:01:00.920
On day 21, close politely. Say this is your last message for now, and that you would be glad to help later.

11
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:08.210
After 60 to 90 days, a new trigger like a new branch gives you a natural reason to return.

12
00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.380
'Just checking in' asks the reader to do work for you. Each message should give her something.

13
00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:21.780
For example, Ngozi, the bookkeeper, messages a pharmacy owner on 3 March. No reply.

14
00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:28.110
Her day 4 reminder gets an answer: 'Not now, very busy with stock taking.'

15
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:39.170
She replies calmly: 'Understood. Shall I check back after your stock taking, perhaps early April?' The owner says yes, and Ngozi notes the date in her sheet.

16
00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:47.310
On 2 April she sends a one-page checklist of records a pharmacy should keep, and asks for a 10-minute call.

17
00:01:48.560 --> 00:02:03.220
On the call she qualifies with BANT and proposes a 3-month clean-up at about 60,000 naira a month, an illustrative price. The owner pays a 50% deposit. Without the follow-up, that 'not now' would have been forgotten.

18
00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:18.820
Small, specific, true claims persuade better than 'best' or 'guaranteed'. Say 'I have done bookkeeping for two clinics and a supermarket', not 'many big companies'. Ask permission before using a client's name, words or logo.

19
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:37.200
Never write reviews yourself, invent urgency, or promise results you do not control. And when someone says 'please stop', stop at once. Mark them 'do not contact' and remove their number, in the spirit of the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.

20
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:48.500
Track five numbers every Friday: contacted, replied, calls, proposals, won. Each rate is one stage divided by the stage just before it.

21
00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:55.870
For example, Halima contacted 40 schools and 14 replied. That is 35%.

22
00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.710
She held 5 calls from those 14 replies, about 36%.

23
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.170
She sent 4 proposals and won 2. Her proposals and messages are working well.

24
00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:21.210
So her weak stage is turning replies into calls. Her one change: offer two specific times instead of 'let me know when you are free'. Change one thing, and test it for 2 to 4 weeks.

25
00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:28.990
Also track your time. Halima spends about 6 hours a week, so 24 hours a month, on outreach.

26
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:37.300
Each new school pays about 45,000 naira for the trial, then about 80,000 naira for the following month.

27
00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.240
Two clients means two of each.

28
00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:54.250
That is about 250,000 naira of work from 24 hours of outreach, roughly 10,400 naira per outreach hour. Outreach is valuable work, not wasted time.

29
00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:08.490
So remember. Follow up four times, adding value each time. If someone says it is too expensive, offer a smaller scope rather than cutting your rate. Stay honest, and stop the moment someone asks.

30
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.150
Small numbers jump around, so collect a month of data before you judge.

31
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.830
Now write your follow-up messages, check your claims, and set up your tracker.

32
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.130
Continue with the lessons below.
